exactly that inertness: `check_asset_catalogue_contract.py` now does carry a rule-id-keyed reader
and a computed `effective_severity`, verified read-only by the KĀRAKA. If that is the same fix,
D-39's F-T36-3 finding may have been written without incorporating it.

It correctly declined to adjudicate whether a ruling used stale evidence — not a KĀRAKA's call —
and recorded the tension rather than picking a reading. Whichever way it resolves doesn't move
D-38/D-39/D-42's classifications, but it bears directly on D-40's flip condition, since the
two-direction fixture proving the mechanism "demonstrably in effect" hasn't been built either way.

